{
  "schema": "alpha60-stage10-kickoff-forecast/1",
  "methods": {
    "time": "Kickoff calendar date is day one. Freeze at the end of date seven (offset six). The daily data do not resolve kickoff hour or local timezone differences.",
    "cohort": "Selected 21 Stage 4/6 fixtures. Retain only canonical full-match releases with a daily cache by the cutoff. Freeze the same releases for both windows. Match tagging is retrospective. Deduplicate raw aliases and IPs across all selected releases within a fixture.",
    "outcome": "For each fixture, early is distinct observed downloader IPs on days 1–7. Added is the IP union on days 8–28 minus the early set. Unknown countries stay in the world denominator. Repeated IPs across fixtures can contribute to each fixture.",
    "network": "Published Stage 4 frozen country and privacy lookups. Remove hosting and VPN addresses separately, recalculating national and worldwide counts for each exclusion.",
    "sample": "A complete observation requires archive coverage on all 28 calendar dates and daily observations for every frozen release from first discovery onward. R32 is specific to the 48-team format. The common-round sample comprises R16, QF, SF and F.",
    "fixed_rules": "At day seven, predict each national share of future additions from that fixture’s own early share. A constant-new-arrival pace predicts three times the first-week unique count over the next 21 days. These rules require no fitted labels. MAE weights fixtures equally; volume-weighted MAE weights by later worldwide additions.",
    "training": "Require the preceding round and outcome_end on or before the forecast cutoff for an operational baseline. The separate earlier-round hindcast uses only earlier-round fixtures, but intentionally allows outcomes that matured after the cutoff. For volume it estimates prior total additions per release or per early IP. For share it uses the unweighted mean of earlier fixture shares.",
    "scenarios": "Low, base and high are empirical 25th, 50th and 75th percentiles of individual complete 2026 common-round fixtures. They are descriptive transfer scenarios, not predictive intervals or evidence of 2027 demand. National percentiles are calculated independently."
  },
